os-builder (3.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Installer: editor for Subiquity's autoinstall.yaml (also read by the
    Ubuntu Desktop installer): guided, partly or fully automatic installs,
    language, keyboard, time zone, user (password stored as SHA-512 hash),
    disk layout and encryption, SSH, updates, drivers, codecs, packages,
    snaps, late-commands, extra YAML; load/save, preview, and a check
    against Subiquity's published JSON schema.
  * Look & feel: GTK, icon and cursor themes from a catalog verified against
    the 26.04 packages, or from theme archives (tar/zip, checked against
    path traversal); applied to GNOME, Budgie, Unity, MATE, Cinnamon and,
    for icons, KDE Plasma; cursor theme for every desktop.
  * Login screen: background, logo and message for GDM, LightDM Slick and
    GTK greeters, SDDM Breeze and greetd/tuigreet.
  * Boot splash: Plymouth theme generated from a logo and a colour, with
    progress bar, passphrase prompt and messages; the live ISO's initrd is
    extended with it, so it also shows when booting the ISO.
  * Bootloader: GRUB background image and colours on the ISO (works with
    Secure Boot), a text editor for boot/grub/grub.cfg, and the installed
    system's menu timeout, kernel arguments and theme (/etc/default/grub.d).
  * The Wizard is split into tabs with image previews.

 -- hugomonizdorego <hugomonizdorego@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0700

os-builder (3.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Renamed from Ubuntu Builder to OS Builder (package os-builder,
    commands os-builder and os-builder-cli, polkit action
    org.os-builder.helper). Replaces and conflicts with ubuntu-builder.
  * Desktop catalog checked against Ubuntu 26.04: GNOME 50, GNOME
    Flashback, KDE Plasma 6.6, Xfce 4.20, LXQt, MATE, Budgie 10.10,
    Cinnamon 6.4, Unity, Edubuntu, Ubuntu Studio, Ubuntu Kylin, LXDE,
    Enlightenment.
  * Wayland compositors: Hyprland 0.53, Sway 1.11, labwc 0.9, Wayfire 0.10,
    each with a working toolkit (foot, fuzzel, waybar, mako, portals).
  * X11 window managers: i3, Openbox, awesome, bspwm, Qtile, xmonad,
    herbstluftwm, IceWM, Fluxbox.
  * Login managers: GDM 50, SDDM 0.21, LightDM with Slick or GTK greeter,
    greetd with tuigreet, LXDM, XDM; set as display-manager.service and
    preseeded through debconf.
  * Desktop button: Sway, labwc and Wayfire run nested in the Xephyr window;
    a clear message for GNOME 49+ and Hyprland, which cannot be nested.
  * UEFI: boot report (legacy BIOS, UEFI, Secure Boot with an Authenticode
    check of the shim), new UEFI-only build mode for modern PCs without
    CSM, new "boot-info" command, QEMU test with Secure Boot enabled.
  * Distribution names may contain "/" (e.g. "DebION GNU/Linux"); new
    workspaces default to the en_US.UTF-8 locale.

 -- hugomonizdorego <hugomonizdorego@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0700

os-builder (3.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Complete rewrite of Ubuntu Builder 2.5.2 in Python 3.12+ and Qt 6.
  * Same workflow and window as Ubuntu Builder 2.x: Select ISO, Wizard,
    Build, QEMU, Export, Remove, Settings; Console, Synaptic, Desktop,
    Install .deb.
  * Releases, support status, flavors and ISO images fetched live from
    ubuntu.com; downloads with resume and SHA-256 verification.
  * Layered squashfs images (Ubuntu 23.04 and later).
  * Hybrid BIOS/UEFI ISO with Secure Boot, built with xorriso from the
    source image's boot records (replaces genisoimage).
  * Background threads with progress and cancel; every mount is released
    on errors and cancellation.
  * Administrator rights through pkexec and polkit instead of gksudo.
  * The history of Ubuntu Builder 0.1 - 2.5.2 is kept in
    legacy/2.5.2/debian/changelog of the source tree.

 -- hugomonizdorego <hugomonizdorego@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0700
